{
 "_about": "Job titles as résumés write them, with the tech role family each must be read as (null: none of the tech roles). The résumé-side twin of evals/titles_tech.json and the tech counterpart of evals/resume_titles.json. Rows marked from_sample are titles (and the employer line beside them) as the published tech résumé samples write them; the rest are the edges the rules must hold, written from the posting spec, not from the reader's output. A résumé has no employer industry, so a bare 'Engineer' or 'Designer' reads as the role. 'known_gap' marks a case the title rules cannot read yet, with its reason: it is reported and not counted, and it stops being a gap the day it passes. 'level' (associate, mid, senior or lead) is the level the title's grade must be read as. Checked by node evals/run_tech.mjs with the role families of web/data/roles_tech.json.",
